  "note": "Relevance = size of the saving (High >=10% of energy, Medium >=3%), a rule applied to SIMULATED savings, so this measures re-learning a rule from visible features, not agreement with real assessors. Heat pump, solar and boiler are near-constant classes, so the headline numbers are 'informative_measures_only'. The ceiling is set by hidden simulator state (thermostat setting, 'assumed' walls that are really insulated); metered-usage features recover part of it, and the monthly-shape features (per-home slope of use against heating degree days, base load, winter/summer ratio) recover more because they reflect the home's true heat-loss response. 'with_abstention' keeps the ~80% most confident predictions (threshold fitted on val) and returns 'needs survey' for the rest. It does NOT predict what the EPC recommends (that is the model below)."
 },
