  "note": "Price LEVEL model: predicts log price RELATIVE to the council's public UK HPI average for the home type (July 2026, greenhome/reference/council_hpi_2026-07.csv), from size, type, age and location relative to the council centre. Without that market-level anchor, home features alone could not tell the model that Liverpool is cheaper than every training city (median error 48%, ranking near random); with it, error on the unseen city is much lower but still higher than in known cities, so treat the level as indicative. HPI values are council averages, not data about any held-out home. The product uses the model for the RELATIVE rating premium; the baseline value is the dataset's current_value_estimate. The rating premium is itself heterogeneous: see premium_by_council_train and heldout_premium_check. The dataset's 4.2% is fitted on all sales including Liverpool/Cardiff, which have higher premiums than the training councils, hence our lower train-only estimate; the range includes a council-level cluster bootstrap to reflect this.",
